{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJust back from the most incredible trip to Japan! It was a whirlwind of ancient traditions and futuristic technology, a truly captivating contrast.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a dazzling metropolis. I spent days exploring vibrant Shibuya Crossing, getting lost in the electric atmosphere of Akihabara, and finding serenity in the Meiji Jingu Shrine. The food was phenomenal – from Michelin-starred ramen to tiny, hole-in-the-wall sushi spots, every meal was an adventure.\n\nNext up was Kyoto, a city steeped in history. Wandering through the bamboo forest of Arashiyama felt like stepping into another world. I visited countless temples and shrines, each more beautiful than the last, and even participated in a traditional tea ceremony. The geishas gracefully gliding through Gion were a magical sight.\n\nBeyond the big cities, I took a day trip to Nara, famous for its friendly wild deer roaming freely in Nara Park. Feeding them crackers was a highlight!\n\nThe bullet train was an experience in itself – smooth, efficient, and incredibly fast. Navigating the public transport system was surprisingly easy, even with my limited Japanese.\n\nJapan is a country that truly stimulates all the senses. It’s a place where politeness and respect are deeply ingrained, and where the beauty of nature is celebrated. I left feeling inspired, refreshed, and already planning my return. Highly recommend adding Japan to your bucket list!\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011843579122796655}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.16028544306755066}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0018123644404113293}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.14268149435520172}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.07544055581092834